{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I will make you a great nation.</b> Even though your wife is barren, as it is written above, 'ותהי שרי עקרה.' Another interpretation: it is not written 'ואשימך' but <b>ואעשך</b>, to say: from the fact that I am making you a new creation, you are fertile and increase. For at first Abraham lacked five things: eyes, ears, and the head of the membrum, as our Rabbis said. And HaShem added to him the letter he in his name, corresponding to five matters in which he was completed through it." "<b>And I will make great your name.</b> With one letter, to the count of 248; thus a complete name and a complete body." "<b>And be a blessing.</b> Blessing shall be found in everything you do, as in 'בימים ההם אשים את ירושלים ברכה בקרב הארץ' (Zechariah 12:3, Isaiah 19:24)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:56.769037477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}